        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "399b89af-a770-53a1-9b7c-9f3466260368",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Dubai, Bur Dubai, Deira, Dubai Creek, Jumeirah Village, United Arab Emirates\n- Markets: Dubai Textile Souk, Old Textile Souk, Dubai Spice Souk, Dubai Gold Souk\n- Religious Sites: Iranian Mosque, Ali ibn Abi Talib Iranian Mosque\n- Buildings: Nili Tower\n- Topics: textile products, jewellery retail, abra boats\n\nFacts:\n- The Dubai Textile Souk, also known as the Old Textile Souk, is a traditional textile market in the historic Bur Dubai neighbourhood of Dubai.\n- The Dubai Spice Souk and Dubai Gold Souk are located in Deira on the opposite side of Dubai Creek from the Dubai Textile Souk.\n- Special abra boats provide access across Dubai Creek between the area of the Dubai Textile Souk and the souks in Deira.\n- The Dubai Gold Souk has over 300 retailers, most of whom are jewellery traders.\n- The Iranian Mosque, also known as the Ali ibn Abi Talib Iranian Mosque, is a Shia mosque near the old Textile Souk in Bur Dubai, Dubai, United Arab Emirates.\n- The Nili Tower is a 57-floor tower in Jumeirah Village in Dubai, United Arab Emirates.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "497ab926-9780-560a-a818-0bce2ab13a70",
        "text": "Page: Dubai Textile Souk. Sentence: The Dubai Textile Souk (Arabic: سوق الغزل والنسيج‎ ‎ ; also known as the Old Textile Souk) is a traditional souq (market) of textile products located in Dubai's historic Bur Dubai neighbourhood.\nPage: Dubai Textile Souk. Sentence: Opposite to the textile souk on the other side of the Dubai Creek lie the Dubai Spice Souk and Dubai Gold Souk in Deira, accessible via the creek by special abra boats.\nPage: Dubai Gold Souk. Sentence: The souk consists of over 300 retailers, most of whom are jewellery traders.\nPage: Iranian Mosque, Bur Dubai. Sentence: The Iranian Mosque (also known as the Ali ibn Abi Talib Iranian Mosque) is a Shia mosque located near the old Textile Souk in the Bur Dubai district of Dubai, United Arab Emirates.\nPage: Nili Tower. Sentence: The Nili Tower is a 57-floor tower in the Jumeirah Village in Dubai, United Arab Emirates.",
